# K03 S7: in a callable merge the group `(y: k)` holds a field, no one value: it is an anonymous Structure operand,
# not the bare `y: k` the callable merge binds -- refused at the group as a form not lowered.
fn: add3 (int: y; int: x; int: z) int
    return: y + x * 10 + z * 100

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x; int: z) int
    return: merge(add3; (y: k))

@: w wrap(5)
int: a (w: 1 2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a - 208; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
